1
00:00:01,700 --> 00:00:04,000
Graduate School staff signs in.

2
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:11,500
The AWOL and Residency board flags cases from imported enrollment records. Nobody types AWOL.

3
00:00:11,699 --> 00:00:19,100
Maya Torres's card sits in AWOL, Waiting for: Student. Staff cannot move it; only the student can start a return.

4
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:27,300
Residence limits apply: master's, five years normal and seven absolute; doctorate, seven and nine. Leave time counts.

5
00:00:28,399 --> 00:00:34,799
The card shows the AWOL date, the flag's source and the last enrolled semester.

6
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:37,299
Maya signs in.

7
00:00:38,299 --> 00:00:42,899
The Return from AWOL page shows the flag. Registration stays restricted until review.

8
00:00:46,299 --> 00:00:51,299
Maya picks the return semester and last enrolled semester, and writes the reason.

9
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:57,799
Submitted. The system checks that Maya is within the maximum residence.

10
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:04,399
Graduate School staff signs in.

11
00:01:04,599 --> 00:01:09,599
On the staff board, the card moves itself to Return review.

12
00:01:09,799 --> 00:01:13,799
The request shows the intention and the residence limits.

13
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:23,700
Graduate School staff forwards it to the Dean with a note.

14
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:28,099
The Dean signs in.

15
00:01:36,599 --> 00:01:43,299
The Dean drags the card to Back in the program. Approval restores standing.

16
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:44,700
Maya is active.

17
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:51,799
Graduate School staff signs in.

18
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:57,399
The Academic Coordinator is next owner, since enrollment is a separate step.

19
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:05,099
The Registrar list holds one report per approved return, downloaded and sent officially.

20
00:02:06,099 --> 00:02:11,500
Maya signs in.

21
00:02:11,699 --> 00:02:18,100
Maya sees the approval. Leave, return and AWOL all run on the same board, request window and Registrar list.
